Also: is the DSH process name exactly "DeepSeek Harness"? Yes from earlier Get-Process list: "DeepSeek Harness".

Also should the watcher handle the case where DSH restarts quickly (user quits and immediately relaunches)? Script polls every 2s; if user reopens fast, process reappears and script waits more. Fine — but then it'd wait until they quit again within 20min. Instruct user: 退出后等 30 秒再打开.

Also: risk - if user quits DSH and the app isn't actually gone (background tray), the script waits. We'll tell them.

Let me verify pwsh path and launch.

Also: after script runs, it relaunches DSH; the user's GUI URL will change port again.

One concern: script's rename of $oldProj while... fine.

Another: script deletes stale copy D:\Work\_stale... (3GB) — takes a while but fine.

Also note: it deletes junction AFTER rewriting headers, good.

