The rename should succeed since DSH exited (no handles). Accept.

Actually safer: if rename fails, fall back to moving child session dirs individually into newProj. Let me update script? Simpler: if oldProj exists and newProj missing and rename fails → create newProj and move children. Add that. Let me edit the script to add fallback.

Edit: replace the rename block with:

if (-not (Test-Path $newProj)) {
  if (Test-Path $oldProj) {
    try { Rename-Item ...; L } catch { L "WARN: rename failed: ..."; }
  }
}
if (-not (Test-Path $newProj)) { New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $newProj | Out-Null; L "created $newProj" }
if (Test-Path $oldProj) {
  foreach ($sd in Get-ChildItem $oldProj -Directory) { $t=Join-Path $newProj $sd.Name; if(-not (Test-Path $t)){ Move-Item ... } }
  if empty -> remove old
}

That covers both. Let me update with edit.

